Closes the read/write asymmetry: poster-vision-extraction already governs reading
text from images (scar 2026-08-27), but no cross-cutting rule governed WRITING
text into artifacts. Generative models estimate glyphs and misspell or invent them
(observed same session: IRFANGLAW, arifeOS, an unrequested watermark); deterministic
renders of the same content: 0 misspellings.

- forge-pdf-delivery: new 'Routing: text vs mood' section (before Pipeline).
  Points at existing partial patterns rather than duplicating them.
- civic-social-infographic: extend the existing matplotlib/HTML+CSS rule to all text.

Gate: verify from the text layer (pdftotext), never from a vision model's opinion.

Proposed by irfanclaw (KVM4). Verified by HERMES. Sealed by ARIF (F13) — NOT YET.
APEX: G=0.823, C_dark=0.0088, verdict OK (is_canonical_g=true; W3 UNMEASURED).

Root-cause note: my first draft targeted a 23-day-stale mirror (39 lines). The real
tree was 2666 commits ahead. Corrected against origin/main before writing.
